  "notes": "The prayer Leo XIII composed and assigned to be said after low Mass; it stands fourth among his prayers, after the Salve Regína and the collect. ÍMPERET at w015 carries its accent on the antepenult, which witness do omits as it omits accents on capitals throughout. Three petitions: a plea for defence, a wish that God command him, and a call to Michael himself — TUQUE opens it, and stands with the sentence it begins. ESTO at w013 is the FUTURE imperative of sum — the form that lays a standing duty rather than an immediate one — and names Collatinus alone, Whitaker's not offering the tense. MÍCHAËL at w002 names Collatinus alone, as every form of the name does in this corpus. TUQUE at w020 is the nominative pronoun with the enclitic -que; the pronoun is expressed at all only because the sentence turns from God back to Michael. CÆLÉSTIS at w023 is genitive, agreeing with milítiæ, not nominative with Princeps. PERVAGÁNTUR at w032 and DEPRECÁMUR at w019 are deponents: passive in form, active in meaning.",
